From 0c9c002008c264c8e27775866f0ca5136a80357a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiangSu8899 <7thuniversels@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:08:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] cuda: FlashRT SM120 fusion windows, NVFP4 quantize
 target, per-shape graph slots

Host side of the FlashRT ggml adapter for the SM120 / Qwen3.6 target:

- ggml-cuda: GGML_CUDA_FLASHRT_SM120 option compiles the adapter's window
  translation unit and the two csrc kernels it needs from a FlashRT
  checkout (GGML_CUDA_FLASHRT_PUBLIC_DIR). The fuse-hook call sites in
  ggml-cuda.cu are compiled out unless the option is on.
- llama-quantize: expose NVFP4 as a quantization target
  (LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_NVFP4 -> GGML_TYPE_NVFP4).
- llama-context: LLAMA_GRAPH_SLOTS=N keeps one reusable graph and
  scheduler per (n_tokens, graph type, embd) shape so speculative decode
  alternating 1-token draft and 4-token verify evals stops rebuilding
  the graph every step. Default 1 preserves stock behaviour.
- test-backend-ops: Qwen3-8B Q4_K_M M=1 GEMV worklist in the perf set.
